cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this material, please cite it as below."
title: "MIP Modelling: mixed-integer linear models for Management Engineering"
abstract: >-
  A course on modelling with integer and binary variables: general techniques
  (logic and binary variables, links between variables, big-M, dual bounds of
  the linear relaxation, constructive heuristics) and six families of problems
  — assignment and scheduling, location and covering, production and lot sizing,
  selection and knapsack, partitioning and balancing, logistics — with solved
  exercises, additional modelling questions, Python/Gurobi code and notebooks.
